<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  JawaAppearance_Tuning.xml                  Jawa_Patches · authored 2026-08-10
  ============================================================================

  Three player-facing appearance decisions, all observed in-game 2026-08-10
  after FA per-xenotype exclusion finally let gene appearance render at all.

  ==========================================================================
  1. "ink black" skin is actually dark grey
  ==========================================================================
  Biotech's Skin_InkBlack declares <skinColorOverride>(55, 55, 55)</>, which
  reads as charcoal, not ink. Set to true black.

  ⚠️ SCOPE: this is a Core Biotech gene shared by 13 active xenotypes, not just
  Jawa: AG_Forsaken, AG_Lapis, AG_Wretch, BS_FireJotun, BS_Svartalf,
  BTD_Aqualish, BTD_Herglic, BTD_Jawa, OuterRim_Aqualish, OuterRim_Herglic and
  three more. All of them are "should look black" xenotypes, so the change is
  an improvement across the board rather than a Jawa-only hack. Say so out loud
  because it is a wider blast radius than the rest of this file.

  ⚠️ (0,0,0) is a deliberate extreme. RimWorld still applies its own shading,
  but pure black loses almost all surface detail and can read as a silhouette.
  If it looks like a hole rather than a creature, raise it to about (15,15,15)
  and the detail comes back while still reading as black.

  ==========================================================================
  2. Jawa had spider eyes and a fanged mouth on top of the yellow eyes
  ==========================================================================
  Observed: correct glowing yellow eyes AND a second set of arachnid eyes AND a
  mouth full of fangs. Cause is not a stray gene, it is the HEAD TEXTURE.
  BTD_Jawa carries Outland_GreaterGoblinoidHead, which forces the head types
  Outland_Male_Goblinoid / Outland_Female_Goblinoid, and that art has its own
  eyes and teeth baked in. The eye gene then draws on top, so you get both.

  Removing the head gene leaves a plain head under the hood with only the
  glowing eyes on it, which is the canonical Jawa read: the face is never seen,
  just two lights in the dark.

  Alternatives if a plain head is too plain. Outland ships these, all usable by
  swapping the removed gene for one of them:
      Outland_RattyHead        Outland_LesserGoblinoidHead
      Outland_SvelteHead       Outland_MonocularHead
      Outland_TrencherHead     Outland_MothHead
  RattyHead and LesserGoblinoidHead are the closest fits for a small hooded
  scavenger and are the two worth trying first.

  ==========================================================================
  3. Jawa spawn male-only for this playthrough
  ==========================================================================
  Player decision, not a bug fix. Outland Genetics already ships Outland_AllMale
  ("all male"), so no new def is needed. Alternatives, if Outland is ever
  dropped: Body_MaleOnly (Big and Small Framework) or AG_Male (Alpha Genes).

  ==========================================================================
  SAFETY AND LOAD ORDER
  ==========================================================================
  Every op is conditional on the exact node, so each becomes a silent no-op if
  a mod update changes the gene list. BTD_Jawa is defined by Xenotype REMIX at
  load 557 and we are 561, so we patch after it exists.

  Ops 2 and 3 use text() predicates on <li> entries, which RimWorld's XPath
  supports but validate_patch.py cannot evaluate. Both were hand-verified
  against the resolved load set on 2026-08-10.

  VERIFY AFTER THE NEXT LOAD
  ==========================
    * Fresh Jawa: black skin, glowing yellow eyes, NO second eye set, NO fangs.
    * All newly generated Jawa are male.
    * The other 12 ink-black xenotypes are darker; check one is not now a
      featureless silhouette.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Patch>

  <!-- ==================================================================
       1. True black ink skin (Core Biotech gene, 13 xenotypes affected)
       ================================================================== -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/GeneDef[defName="Skin_InkBlack"]/skinColorOverride</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationReplace">
      <xpath>/Defs/GeneDef[defName="Skin_InkBlack"]/skinColorOverride</xpath>
      <value>
        <skinColorOverride>(0, 0, 0)</skinColorOverride>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

  <!-- ==================================================================
       2. Drop the goblinoid head from Jawa (removes spider eyes + fangs)
       ================================================================== -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/XenotypeDef[defName="BTD_Jawa"]/genes/li[text()="Outland_GreaterGoblinoidHead"]</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationRemove">
      <xpath>/Defs/XenotypeDef[defName="BTD_Jawa"]/genes/li[text()="Outland_GreaterGoblinoidHead"]</xpath>
    </match>
  </Operation>

  <!-- ==================================================================
       3. Jawa are male-only this playthrough
       ================================================================== -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/XenotypeDef[defName="BTD_Jawa"]/genes[not(li[text()="Outland_AllMale"])]</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>/Defs/XenotypeDef[defName="BTD_Jawa"]/genes[not(li[text()="Outland_AllMale"])]</xpath>
      <value>
        <li>Outland_AllMale</li>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
